.TH AMETHYSTC 1 "October 2026" "Amethyst 1.2.0" "Amethyst Manual"
.SH NAME
amethystc \- compile Amethyst programs to native x86-64 binaries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amethystc
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile.amt\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amethystc
is the Amethyst Dev Kit compiler. It type-checks a \fI.amt\fR source file,
emits GNU as x86-64 assembly, assembles it with
.BR as (1),
and links a native executable with the system C linker (for libc/\fBprintf\fR
used by \fBprint\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o \fIpath\fR
Output path for the executable (default: a.out). With \fB\-S\fR, path of the
.emitted .s file.
.TP
.B \-S
Emit assembly only; do not assemble or link.
.TP
.B \-\-emit\-asm
Keep intermediate \fI.s\fR and \fI.o\fR files next to the input (debugging).
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Show usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create and run a starter program:
.PP
.RS
.nf
amethyst-new hello
amethystc hello.amt -o hello
./hello
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect generated assembly:
.PP
.RS
.nf
amethystc -S hello.amt -o hello.s
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/amethyst/examples
Example Amethyst programs.
.TP
.I /usr/share/amethyst/templates
Templates used by
.BR amethyst-new (1).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/amethyst/README.md
Language overview and reference.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B amethystc
exits 0 on success, 1 on compile/link errors. Runtime exit status of the
produced program is the value returned by \fBmain\fR (mod 256).
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Errors use the form
.IB file : line : col : error: message
on stderr.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amethyst-new (1),
.BR as (1),
.BR gcc (1),
.BR ld (1)
